Break tests — Phase 20c, the page reads the suites and a node answers for its own step
Run on 2026-08-08 in the chat session's own clone, offline: no AWS, no cost.

Ten deliberate defects, with a green control before the first and after the
last. Every one was restored with `git checkout` and the page rebuilt, and the
final control shows a clean tree.

Numbers 6, 8 and 10 are the defects this session FIXED, put back on purpose:
6 is the node in a running phase that claimed to be running itself, 8 is the
suite that inherited its phase instead of asking its own step - the shape that
left suite.db.stage dark while its step ran - and 10 is the phase clock that
restarted every time the apply moved to the next bound step. 7 is finding two
inverted: with the completed-run guard removed, a finished run keeps saying
"finished in this run" over the top of the figures it published.

One thing that broke without being planned, before this log was taken: the gate
reads the BUILT page, so an edit to assets/index.template.html that had not been
rebuilt made it fail against the previous build. That is site-page-check's
property arriving here for free, and it is how the first run of these fixtures
went red.


